WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.800
Cloud PKI is a Microsoft-hosted PKI
managed in the Intune admin center.

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.111
It hosts the root and issuing CAs,

3
00:00:08.111 --> 00:00:11.707
a SCEP registration authority
for each issuing CA,

4
00:00:11.707 --> 00:00:17.100
the CRL distribution point and the AIA
endpoint, which together replace the

5
00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:22.750
on-premises CA, NDES server and Certificate
Connector for device certificates.

6
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:23.700
What it can do.

7
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:28.369
Issue client-authentication certificates
to Intune-enrolled Android,

8
00:00:28.369 --> 00:00:30.937
Apple and Windows devices, through SCEP.

9
00:00:30.937 --> 00:00:33.875
Publish a CRL per CA, valid seven days,

10
00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:39.063
republished every three and a half
days and on every revocation.

11
00:00:39.063 --> 00:00:41.437
And host up to three CAs per tenant.

12
00:00:41.437 --> 00:00:42.363
What it can't.

13
00:00:42.363 --> 00:00:48.202
Issue to anything not enrolled in Intune;
Intune doesn't support Windows Server,

14
00:00:48.202 --> 00:00:50.768
so no domain controller, NPS server,

15
00:00:50.768 --> 00:00:54.662
web server or SQL Server gets
a Cloud PKI certificate.

16
00:00:54.662 --> 00:00:59.276
Issue the server certificates
RADIUS and VPN gateways present;

17
00:00:59.276 --> 00:01:02.670
Microsoft says those must
come from another CA.

18
00:01:02.670 --> 00:01:04.063
Issue through PKCS.

19
00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:05.675
Answer OCSP.

20
00:01:05.675 --> 00:01:08.600
And change a CA's EKUs after creation.

21
00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.488
Plan the three-CA count
before you create anything.

22
00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:14.543
Keys: licensed CAs use Azure Managed HSM;

23
00:01:14.543 --> 00:01:19.637
trial CAs use software keys that
can't be converted after purchase.

24
00:01:19.637 --> 00:01:25.226
Licensing: Cloud PKI is a subscription
on top of Intune Plan 1 or 2.

25
00:01:25.226 --> 00:01:30.486
From July 2026, Microsoft 365 E5 and E7
include it for commercial customers;

26
00:01:30.486 --> 00:01:35.917
Microsoft says Government plans are
planned to align, subject to compliance

27
00:01:35.917 --> 00:01:41.263
and regulatory requirements, so confirm
the entitlement on the current SKU.

28
00:01:41.263 --> 00:01:45.394
And availability: GCC uses
the commercial Intune service,

29
00:01:45.394 --> 00:01:49.525
so availability follows it
and licensing is the question.

30
00:01:49.525 --> 00:01:55.421
Cloud PKI became available in GCC
High in the week of September 28,

31
00:01:55.421 --> 00:01:58.200
2026, and isn't supported in DoD.
